      "title": "Project Progress Desk consolidates multi-agent coding sessions into one view",
      "summary": "Researchers introduced Project Progress Desk, a desktop interface aggregating multiple parallel coding agents from Claude Code and Codex. The tool replaces fragmented terminal windows with a consolidated view of agent progress, blockers, and required human approvals.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Aggregates parallel agent sessions across Claude Code and Codex.",
        "Surfaces active blockers and pending decisions in a single view.",
        "Replaces manual tab switching across separate chats and terminals."
      ],
      "design_implication": "When developers and designers run multiple autonomous agents simultaneously, tab-based chat windows fail to communicate which processes require urgent intervention. Oversight shifts from reading continuous log streams to triaging discrete status flags, decision requests, and blocked dependencies across concurrent threads. Design multi-agent management consoles around state summaries and action prompts rather than raw, real-time command line feeds.",
      "implication_lens": "pattern",
      "visual_need": "illustrate",
      "source_name": "arXiv cs.HC",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.13287",
      "source_date": "2026-11-11T05:00:00.000Z",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "claim": "Project Progress Desk unifies parallel Codex and Claude Code projects into a single view.",
          "quote": "We present Project Progress Desk, a local desktop interface that brings overall progress, blockers and pending decisions into one view."
        },
